notes.body:
So I'd say, for now:

- for MSVC, assume unaligned accesses are safe for x86 32-bit and 64-bit (and maybe for ARM64 as well), and don't just use shifts and masks;
- for icc - which, as one might guess, is x86-only - assume unaligned accesses are safe for x86 32-bit and 64-bit, and don't just use shifts and masks;
- for everything else, just use shifts and masks and let the compiler optimize it.

